<title>USA: Top 25 manufacturers by revenue - survey.</title>
<headline>Top 25 manufacturers by revenue - survey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top manufacturing companies by revenue, according to IndustryWeek magazine, which compiled the list with Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp. and Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p> Company		   Country     Revenue	 Net Income</p>
<p>					     in billions   in billions</p>
<p>								 unless stated</p>
<p> General Motors Corp.  U.S.	  $164	   $4.96</p>
<p> Ford Motor Co.	  U.S.	  $147	   $4.45</p>
<p> Royal Dutch Petroleum Netherlands $139	   $9.64</p>
<p> Exxon Corp.	     U.S.	  $134	   $7.51</p>
<p> Mobil Corp.	     U.S.	  $82	    $2.96</p>
<p> General Electric Co.  U.S.	  $79	    $7.28</p>
<p> International Business</p>
<p>  Machines Corp.	 U.S.	  $76	    $5.43</p>
<p> British Petroleum Co. U.K.	  $76	    $4.32</p>
<p> Hitachi Ltd.	    Japan	 $71	    $1.23</p>
<p> Toyota Motor Corp.    Japan	 $71	    $1.15</p>
<p> Daimler-Benz AG	 Germany     $69	    $1.78</p>
<p> Philip Morris Cos.    U.S.	  $69	    $6.30</p>
<p> Volkswagen AG	   Germany     $64	    $436 million</p>
